   "code": "LABEL_ERROR",
   "text": "The 'derived play-type possession records' rely on inferred labels. If these labels contain significant noise or are systematically biased, any observed H2-H1 changes based on them might be an artifact of the labeling process rather than a true reflection of on-court events. Previous work explicitly noted 'near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise'."
  },
  {
   "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
   "text": "Even if an H2-H1 change can be observed, its reliability as a consistent measure of a defensive team's 'trait' is questionable if the underlying measurement is confounded and subject to label error. A noisy and unreliably attributed measure cannot be a reliable trait."
  },
  {
   "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
   "text": "While 120 team-seasons are available, if the within-game H2-H1 effects are subtle and highly variable, and require complex controls to isolate, the effective sample size for reliably measuring a 'trait' (i.e., consistent effect across multiple games/seasons for a given team) might be insufficient to achieve useful statistical power, especially after filtering for meaningful play-type usage."
   }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.05,
  "rejected": 0.1,
  "untestable": 0.7,
  "artifact": 0.1,
  "uncertain": 0.05
 },
 "decision": "do_not_proceed",
